    "file": "harfbuzz/src/hb-ot-cff2-table.hh",
    "description": "Heap-buffer-overflow during CFF2 subsetting is caused by trusting malformed CFF2 VariationStore size/offset metadata from the input font and then memcpy\u2019ing that computed length without validating it against the source blob bounds. In the crashing path, serialize() copies far more bytes than exist in the backing font data (read of ~62017 bytes from a 383-byte region), so the immediate crash is in CFF2VariationStore::serialize, while the root issue is missing bounds/sanity checks on VariationStore-derived lengths before copy in the CFF2 subset write path (_write_cff2 -> serialize).",
    "conditions": "Trigger via hb-subset-fuzzer with a crafted OpenType font containing a CFF2 table whose VariationStore fields encode inconsistent/oversized lengths or offsets. Data flow: fuzzer input bytes -> hb_blob/hb_face -> hb_subset() -> CFF2 subsetting (_hb_subset_cff2/_write_cff2) -> CFF2VariationStore::serialize memcpy using attacker-controlled table metadata. The PoV does not require large input; malformed internal table structure is sufficient."
  },
